ESP-IDF: build an application as the ESP32-S31 radio co-processor firmware

With CONFIG_ESPCP_FIRMWARE (espcp/components/espcp_sys/Kconfig), a
single-core application runs on hart 1 while another OS (NetBSD) runs on
hart 0, so it must not touch what that OS owns:

 - rv_utils_get_core_id() says 0 on hart 1; espcp_sys routes interrupts
   to the hart that is really running.
 - The FreeRTOS tick uses systimer alarm 1 and leaves the systimer itself,
   counter 0 and alarm 0 to the host; esp_timer doesn't reset it either.
 - No flash driver and no partition-table protection: the host owns the
   SPI flash.
 - Panics and restarts report to the host and stop the hart instead of
   resetting the chip (and no RTC watchdog).
 - The image runs in place from its own flash partition, and its RAM
   starts above OpenSBI.

Against ESP-IDF ab95e707 (master, 2026-10).

